.TH CBMAP_CREATE_CH 3 "2026-10-06" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_create_ch \- create a BST map ordered by a custom comparison procedure
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

typedef int (*ccol_comparison_proc_t)(const void *first,
                                      const void *second);

cbmap cbmap_create_ch(ccol_data_type key_type,
                      ccol_comparison_proc_t custom_comparison_proc,
                      char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a self-balancing BST map in which custom_comparison_proc sets the
order of the keys. The function is a thin inline wrapper over
cbmap_create_full(3) that gives NULL for the memory management
procedures, so the map uses the default allocator. The type-inferred
equivalents are cbmap_construct_cc(3) and cbmap_init_cc(3).

The procedure decides the order of the keys and nothing else: key_type
sets the width that the map expects of every key_pair of a fixed-width
key type, and key_type also sets the alignment of every stored key.

cbmap_construct_cc(3) gives the contract of the procedure:
  - It returns a negative value, zero or a positive value.
  - It defines key equality and key order.
  - It must give a consistent, transitive order for the whole life of
    the map.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
key_type                Type of the keys that the map stores
custom_comparison_proc  Comparison procedure, or NULL for the default
                        order for key_type
err                     Optional pointer that receives an error string on
                        failure, or NULL
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new map on success.
NULL on failure, in which case *err is set to an error string when err is
not NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The procedure gets two bare pointers to key bytes, and a key that comes
in through the raw layer can be at any address. Read a key that is wider
than one byte through memcpy, not through a pointer cast to the key type
The procedure must stay callable for the whole life of the map
The function reports a failure instead of stopping the program, while the
cbmap_construct_cc(3) and cbmap_init_cc(3) macros call ccol_fatal_err()
on a failure
Destroy the map with cbmap_destroy(3)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
typedef struct { int major; int minor; } version;

int version_cmp(const void *a, const void *b) {
    version x, y;
    memcpy(&x, a, sizeof(x));
    memcpy(&y, b, sizeof(y));
    if (x.major != y.major) {
        return (x.major > y.major) - (x.major < y.major);
    }
    return (x.minor > y.minor) - (x.minor < y.minor);
}

char *err = NULL;
cbmap releases = cbmap_create_ch(ccol_other_types, version_cmp, &err);
if (!releases) {
    fprintf(stderr, "%s\en", err);
    return 1;
}
/* ... cbmap_insert_elem(releases, ...) ... */
cbmap_destroy(releases);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create (3),
.BR cbmap_create_full (3),
.BR cbmap_construct_cc (3),
.BR cbmap_init_cc (3),
.BR cbmap_destroy (3)
